D166 instrumentation: ADVSI entry/exit dumps. Generated by `diff -u` against the pristine ICEDYN_DRV.f (modelE2_planet_2.0; the original tree is read-only).
Apply to a SCRATCH COPY only:  cd <copy>/model && patch ICEDYN_DRV.f < ICEDYN_DRV_advsi.f.patch   (the file paths in the headers below are not used)
Independent of every other patch (no ATM_DRV change): helpers ffadv_open/ffadv_w2/ffadv_w3 are appended to ICEDYN_DRV.f itself.
Units 1600 (entry) and 1601 (exit), closed after each call; unused by any other patch (1500-1529 are reserved for the persistent radiation server).
Output ffadv_in_<itime>.bin / ffadv_out_<itime>.bin (big-endian float64 stream, layouts in advsi_ff.read_dump) when FFD_START <= itime < FFD_START+FFD_NSTEP.
Build/run as in build_and_run.md (gmake RUN=P2SAoM40 .../P2SAoM40.bin; copy the binary to BOTH P2SAoM40.bin and P2SAoM40; reset fort.1.nc and fort.2.nc
from ff_data/_pristine_restarts). Do not `cp -P` a run directory that contains a FIFO (req.fifo of the radiation server): it blocks forever.

